# ba Windsurf Rules
- Terse, token-efficient communication: no conversational filler, no polite preamble, max 3-5 lines final summary.
- Strict TDD: for new features or security fixes, create tests first (RED), confirm failure, then implement (GREEN).
- Run `bash scripts/prove-test.sh "<cmd>" <test-files>` to prove tests are real (reverts implementation to verify test failure).
- Run `bash scripts/gate.sh .` to ensure compilation, linting, and tests pass with compact logs.
- Preserve existing tests and behavior during refactoring (`bash scripts/prove-refactor.sh origin/main refactor`).
- Comments must only explain non-obvious WHY (workarounds, invariants). Never narrate WHAT code does.
